    "claim": "2026-07-31: memory v0 built (kb + the memory facet + the index fence). A same-day kb/episodic library split was FOLDED BACK within hours — one kb library; the episodic/curated distinction rides naming (month buckets) and tags, not structure",
    "detail": "Two lessons. (1) Modules install before the frame configures the store connection, so store.mode() is null at module scope — anything needing the connection at install time must poll (agent.memory does, before its index prefetch). (2) The split's motivation dissolved the moment everything was git-tracked, and it was executed anyway — when a directive's premise shifts, surface it before building.",
